Subject: [PATCH] 1454 / 2909: an English introduction plan through two
 go-betweens is its one sentence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 54165 (conv 50265): „I'll talk to Levan's and Maia's assistants…" was
not read as the plan sentence (the pattern wanted one word between „talk
to" and „assistant"), so the reply kept the model's paragraphs and asked
for the reason twice; „I approve" then met no plan buttons. The pattern
now reads one go-between or several in en/ru/es, as the Georgian one does,
and the reply is the plan sentence and „Shall I start?". No new text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
